{"product_id":"someday-someday-maybe-a-novel","title":"Someday, Someday, Maybe: A Novel","description":"\u003cp\u003eNEW YORK TIMES BESTSELLER í˘ŚóŚ˘ From Lauren Graham, the beloved star of Gilmore Girls and Parenthood, comes a witty, charming, and hilariously relatable debut novel about a struggling young actress trying to get aheadí˘ŚóŚ´and keep it togetherí˘ŚóŚ´in New York City.Ití˘ŚóŚ»s January 1995, and Franny Banks has just six months left of the three-year deadline she set for herself when she came to New York, dreaming of Broadway and doing í˘ŚóŚěimportantí˘ŚóŚť work. But all she has to show for her efforts so far is a part in an ad for ugly Christmas sweaters, and a gig waiting tables at a comedy club. Her roommatesí˘ŚóŚ´her best friend Jane, and Dan, an aspiring sci-fi writerí˘ŚóŚ´are supportive, yet Franny knows a two-person fan club doesní˘ŚóŚ»t exactly count as success. Everyone tells her she needs a backup plan, and though she can almost picture moving back home and settling down with her perfectly nice ex-boyfriend, sheí˘ŚóŚ»s not ready to give up on her goal of having a career like her idols Diane Keaton and Meryl Streep. Not just yet. But while she dreams of filling their shoes, in the meantime, sheí˘ŚóŚ»d happily settle for a speaking part in almost anythingí˘ŚóŚîand finding a hair product combination that works.Everything is riding on the upcoming showcase for her acting class, where sheí˘ŚóŚ»ll finally have a chance to perform for people who could actually hire her. And she caní˘ŚóŚ»t let herself be distracted by James Franklin, a notorious flirt and the most successful actor in her class, even though heí˘ŚóŚ»s suddenly started paying attention. Meanwhile, her bank account is rapidly dwindling, her father wants her to come home, and her agent doesní˘ŚóŚ»t return her calls. But for some reason, she keeps believing that she just might get what she came for.Someday, Someday, Maybe is a story about hopes and dreams, being young in a city, and wanting something deeply, madly, desperately. Ití˘ŚóŚ»s about finding love, finding yourself, and perhaps most difficult of all in New York City, finding an acting job.Praise for Someday, Someday, Maybeí˘ŚóŚěA winning, entertaining read . . . [Lauren Graham] has smartly mined just the right details from her own experience, infusing her work with crackling dialogue and observations about show business that ring funny and true.í˘ŚóŚťí˘ŚóŚîThe Washington Postí˘ŚóŚěA charmer of a first novel . . . [Graham] has an easy, unforced style and, when the situation calls for it, a keen sense of the ridiculous.í˘ŚóŚťí˘ŚóŚîThe Wall Street Journalí˘ŚóŚěWith insight, care, and an abundance of humor . . . Graham demonstrates that her acting chops are not her only talent.í˘ŚóŚťí˘ŚóŚîLibrary Journalí˘ŚóŚěThoroughly charming.í˘ŚóŚťí˘ŚóŚîEntertainment Weeklyí˘ŚóŚěSweet, funny, and full of heart . . . a dazzling debut.í˘ŚóŚťí˘ŚóŚîEmily Giffin, New York Times bestselling author of Something Borrowed and Where We Belongí˘ŚóŚěWarm and funny, charming and smart.í˘ŚóŚťí˘ŚóŚîDiane Keaton, New York Times bestselling author of Then Againí˘ŚóŚěGraham deftly captures what ití˘ŚóŚ»s like to be young, ambitious, and hopeful in New York City.í˘ŚóŚťí˘ŚóŚîCandace Bushnell, New York Times bestselling author of Sex and the City and The Carrie Diariesí˘ŚóŚěFresh and funny and full of zingers, Lauren Grahamí˘ŚóŚ»s charming writing style instantly drew me in.í˘ŚóŚťí˘ŚóŚîMeg Cabot, bestselling author of the Princess Diaries and Heather Wells Mystery series \u003cbr\u003e\n Dimensions:  \u003cbr\u003e\n Author: Lauren Graham \u003cbr\u003e\n ISBN: 9780345532763 \u003cbr\u003e\n Format: Paperback \u003cbr\u003e\n Pages 368\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookloopbook.com","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45063035814041,"sku":"11RA9780345532763","price":10.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/cb3fe79227192b991a082411b528d0ef.jpg?v=1